#: ../../deprecations/pending-removal-in-3.19.rst:12
msgid ""
"In hash function constructors such as :func:`~hashlib.new` or the direct "
"hash-named constructors such as :func:`~hashlib.md5` and "
":func:`~hashlib.sha256`, their optional initial data parameter could also be"
" passed a keyword argument named ``data=`` or ``string=`` in various "
":mod:`!hashlib` implementations."
msgstr ""
"V konstruktorech hashovaci funkce jako :func:`~hashlib.new` nebo primy hash "
"pojmenovani konstruktory jako :func:`~hashlib.md5` a "
":func:`~hashlib.sha256`, jejich volitelny parametr pocatecnich dat mohl byt "
"take preslany pojmenovany argument pojmenovat ``data=`` nebo ``string=`` v "
"ruznych implementacich :mod:`!hashlib`."

#: ../../deprecations/pending-removal-in-3.19.rst:18
msgid ""
"Support for the ``string`` keyword argument name is now deprecated and "
"slated for removal in Python 3.19."
msgstr ""
"Podpora pro ``string`` jmeno pojmenovaneho argumentu je nyní zastarala a je "
"naplanovana na odebrani v Pythonu 3.19."

#: ../../deprecations/pending-removal-in-3.19.rst:21
msgid ""
"Before Python 3.13, the ``string`` keyword parameter was not correctly "
"supported depending on the backend implementation of hash functions. Prefer "
"passing the initial data as a positional argument for maximum backwards "
"compatibility."
msgstr ""
"Pred Pythonem 3.13 nebyl parametr ``string`` spravne podporovan v zavislosti"
" na implementaci backendu hashovacich funkcí. Uprednostnu preslani "
"pocatecnich dat jako poziicny argument pro maximalní spate kompatibilitu."

